Subject: Break closure self-cycles under deferred counting

What this does
  Break closure self-cycles under deferred counting.

Why we need it
  `var loop = function{ . Loop . }` is a two-object cycle: the cell holds the closure and the closure holds the cell.

What it adds
  `js_closcyc_frame`'s DRC branch records any detached cell that holds its own closure -- the count is NOT tested there, because dead sibling closures over the same cell may still be parked and still hold it. `js_closcyc_resolve` runs at the *end* of `js_drc_reconcile_locked`, after the parked lists are drained and while registers are still pinned, and makes the exact count test there: it breaks a cell whose count is exactly the list's plus the closure's own and whose closure is held only there. `QJS_DRC_CLOSCYC=0` restores the old `continue`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 358ec43..a7f3028 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -125,6 +125,16 @@ typedef struct JSRegRCC JSRegRCC;
 #define QJS_CTOR_PROTO_FAST 1
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * QJS_DRC_CLOSCYC: under deferred reference counting, break a frame's
+ * closure -> cell self-cycle at the next reconcile instead of leaving it to the
+ * full collector. Off restores the old `continue` (every such cycle waits for a
+ * mark-sweep).
+ */
+#ifndef QJS_DRC_CLOSCYC
+#define QJS_DRC_CLOSCYC 1
+#endif
+
